#pragma once

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//  SteamAuthBridge — makes Steam auth-session tickets succeed for games
//  whose matchmaking needs one but which get a failing ticket under the
//  480 AppId spoof.
//
//  Why this exists: some games (e.g. R.E.P.O via Photon) call
//  ISteamUser::GetAuthSessionTicket and hand the bytes to their backend.
//  Facepunch's wrapper returns null when the underlying call yields a
//  zero handle, and the game then dereferences it → NullReferenceException
//  before it ever connects. We hook the flat steam_api64.dll exports
//  in-process (same Detours discipline as EosBridge) and, ONLY when the
//  real call fails, forge a non-empty ticket + post the success callback.
//
//  No-regression by construction: we call the real export first and pass
//  its result through untouched whenever Steam succeeds — so games that
//  already get valid tickets (Steam P2P peer auth, etc.) are unaffected.
//  The forge path engages exclusively on the real-failure case.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

namespace SteamAuthBridge {

    // Hook the auth-ticket flat exports in the already-loaded
    // steam_api64.dll. Idempotent; no-op if steam_api isn't present yet.
    // Call from the payload once Steam's API module is loaded.
    void Install();

} // namespace SteamAuthBridge
